<section xml:id="sec-expressions" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" >
  <title>Java Expressions</title>
<introduction>
<p>
Now that we've been introduced to minimal but complete Java programs as well as the 
tools used to develop them, we'll zoom in to the smallest elements of 
structural programming -- expressions. We've already seen an example of literal 
expressions earlier in this chapter (expressions like "hello" and 8.6). Now 
we'll build more complex expressions that explore Java's innate capabilities 
for arithmetic and manipulation of data. Having a tool like jshell allows us 
to play with simple expressions without needing to write an entire program, 
so feel free to copy/paste examples in to jshell as you continue through
this chapter!
</p>
</introduction>

